  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nUpper level low pressure will continue to exit the region\ntonight with weakening winds. This will allow mtn snow shower\nactivity to end with partly cloudy skies expected overnight. Low\ntemperatures will generally be into the 20s to lower 30s.\n\nThere remains strong agreement in latest global and ensemble\nbased guidance that broad high pressure will build across the\neastern half of the CONUS through much of this week. This will \nresult in mainly dry conditions with warm days and cool nights. \nDaytime highs will likely reach the upper 50s to perhaps lower \n60s some afternoons south of the mtns by mid-week before \nradiational cooling allows for 20-30+ degree diurnal ranges some\ndays. This latest dry stretch will continue to result in growing\nrainfall deficits, worsening the ongoing water resource drought\nthat is impacting much of the region.",
